---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import JcecPhase5Progress from '../../../../../components/JcecPhase5Progress.astro';
import { phase5GeologicalSites } from '../../../../../data/jabberwockyPhase5';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const missions = [
  { number:1, title:'Read the Ground', question:'What can observations of rocks and minerals tell us about a site?', summary:'Learn how geologists gather evidence before making claims.', icon:'🔎', status:'CURRENT', ready:true, href:`${base}courses/grade-7-science/jabberwocky/phase-5/mission-1/`, linkText:'Start Mission 1 →' },
  { number:2, title:'Follow the Rock Story', question:'How can rocks record the processes that formed and changed them?', summary:'Use formation evidence to reconstruct rock history.', icon:'🪨', status:'UPCOMING', ready:false },
  { number:3, title:'Track the Changing Surface', question:'How can small surface processes reshape a landscape over long periods?', summary:'Investigate weathering, erosion, deposition and gradual change.', icon:'💧', status:'UPCOMING', ready:false },
  { number:4, title:'Read the Deep Past', question:'How can layers, landforms and fossils reveal events we never observed?', summary:'Reconstruct past change using accumulated geological evidence.', icon:'🧭', status:'UPCOMING', ready:false },
  { number:5, title:'Prepare the Final Evidence', question:'What geological evidence must JCEC carry into the final Mission 2190 decision?', summary:'Build the geological handoff without making the final settlement decision.', icon:'📁', status:'UPCOMING', ready:false }
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Phase 5: The Deep Record | Mission 2190" description="Phase 5 of Jabberwocky: Mission 2190 — the JCEC Geological Survey Division." themeColor="#111916">
  <div class="phase5-shell" id="phase5-hub">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[
      { label:'Home', href:base },
      { label:'Grade 7 Science', href:`${base}courses/grade-7-science/` },
      { label:'Jabberwocky', href:`${base}courses/grade-7-science/jabberwocky/` },
      { label:'Phase 5' }
    ]} />

    <header class="phase5-hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">MISSION 2190 // FINAL SCIENCE PHASE</p>
        <h1>THE <span>DEEP RECORD</span></h1>
        <p class="division">JCEC GEOLOGICAL SURVEY DIVISION</p>
        <p class="lead">JCEC understands Jabberwocky's ecosystems, living resources, thermal-survival needs and structural requirements. But every proposed habitat still depends on something earlier divisions mostly saw from the surface: <strong>the ground beneath it.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <aside><span>YOUR ROLE</span><strong>Geological Survey Specialist</strong><small>Observe. Test. Infer. Question. Hand off evidence.</small></aside>
    </header>

    <section class="big-question"><span>THE FINAL SCIENCE QUESTION</span><h2>What does the geological evidence tell us about where and how humans could live on Jabberwocky—and what must remain protected?</h2><p>Phase 5 prepares evidence for the future JCEC Council. It does <b>not</b> make the final settlement decision yet.</p></section>

    <JcecPhase5Progress active={1} />

    <section class="posting-panel">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">NEW TEAM · NEW SURVEY</p><h2>Normally, rotate to a new continent again.</h2><p>If practical, your teacher should assign a continent you have not investigated before. At minimum, Phase 5 should not automatically repeat your Phase 4 posting. Save only the continent your teacher assigns.</p></div>
      <div class="assignment-control"><label for="phase5-continent"><strong>Your Phase 5 continent</strong><span>Choose only your teacher-assigned Geological Survey posting.</span></label><select id="phase5-continent"><option value="">Choose your assigned continent…</option>{phase5GeologicalSites.map((site) => <option value={site.id}>{site.icon} {site.name} — {site.subtitle}</option>)}</select><p id="save-message" aria-live="polite"></p></div>
    </section>

    <section class="previous-team" id="previous-team" hidden>
      <div class="briefing-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">PREVIOUS TEAM GEOLOGICAL BRIEFING</p><h2>Four inherited facts. No archive search.</h2></div><strong id="briefing-continent"></strong></div>
      <p class="briefing-intro">Earlier JCEC divisions already learned enough to set limits for this survey. Your team starts with only the evidence that matters now.</p>
      <div class="briefing-grid">
        <article><small>SURFACE / ENVIRONMENT</small><p id="briefing-surface"></p></article>
        <article><small>STRUCTURAL SITE NEED</small><p id="briefing-structure"></p></article>
        <article><small>GROUND-DISTURBANCE LIMIT</small><p id="briefing-ground"></p></article>
        <article><small>OPEN GEOLOGICAL QUESTION</small><p id="briefing-question"></p></article>
      </div>
      <div class="continue-strip"><div><strong>The previous teams are finished. Your problem is different.</strong><span>Mission 1 asks what the surface evidence can actually support before anyone makes geological claims.</span></div><a href={`${base}courses/grade-7-science/jabberwocky/phase-5/mission-1/`}>Start Mission 1 →</a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="quick-start" id="assignment-needed"><div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR NEXT STEP</p><h2>Confirm your Geological Survey posting.</h2><p>Once your assigned continent is saved, your four inherited briefing cards and Mission 1 route are ready.</p></div><span>5</span></section>

    <section class="evidence-system">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">ONE RULE FOR ALL OF PHASE 5</p><h2>Keep two kinds of evidence separate.</h2></div>
      <div class="evidence-grid">
        <article class="earth"><small>EARTH REFERENCE EVIDENCE</small><h3>REAL EARTH · AUTHENTIC SOURCE</h3><p>Use real Earth evidence to learn what geological observations and patterns can mean.</p></article>
        <article class="jabber"><small>JABBERWOCKY SURVEY EVIDENCE</small><h3>MISSION 2190 SURVEY</h3><p>Use only JCEC survey observations when making claims about your assigned continent.</p></article>
      </div>
      <div class="evidence-rule"><strong>Earth Reference Evidence teaches us what evidence can mean.</strong><span>Jabberwocky Survey Evidence tells us what JCEC actually found.</span><b>Do not assume an Earth process exists on Jabberwocky unless Jabberwocky survey evidence supports it.</b></div>
    </section>

    <section class="how-it-works"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">SAME ROUTINE EVERY MISSION</p><h2>How The Deep Record works</h2></div><div class="work-grid"><article>👥 <div><strong>TEAM WORK</strong><p>Investigate one geological question and make one team decision.</p></div></article><article>📝 <div><strong>TEAM RECORD</strong><p>Keep only the evidence the next mission or final Council will need.</p></div></article><article>💭 <div><strong>MY REFLECTION</strong><p>Everyone answers one short science question.</p></div></article></div></section>

    <section class="mission-list">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">PHASE 5 PATH</p><h2>Five missions. One geological handoff.</h2></div>
      <div class="sequence-strip"><span class="current">Evidence ●</span><b>→</b><span>Rock History ○</span><b>→</b><span>Surface Change ○</span><b>→</b><span>Deep Past ○</span><b>→</b><span>Geological Handoff ○</span></div>
      <div class="mission-cards">{missions.map((mission) => <article class:list={['mission-card',{current:mission.number===1,locked:!mission.ready}]}><div class="mission-icon">{mission.icon}</div><div class="mission-main"><div class="mission-topline"><span>MISSION {mission.number}</span><b>{mission.status}</b></div><h3>{mission.title}</h3><p class="mission-question">{mission.question}</p><p class="mission-summary">{mission.summary}</p></div>{mission.ready?<a class="mission-ready-link" href={mission.href}>{mission.linkText}</a>:<span class="mission-locked">🔒 Not released yet</span>}</article>)}</div>
    </section>

    <section class="phase4-link"><span>←</span><div><strong>Coming from Project New Horizon?</strong><p>The four briefing cards above carry forward the structural and ecological limits you need. Students do not need to reopen Phase 4.</p></div><a href={`${base}courses/grade-7-science/jabberwocky/phase-4/mission-5/`}>Review Phase 4 conclusion</a></section>
  </div>

  <script is:inline define:vars={{ siteData: phase5GeologicalSites }}>
    (() => {
      const KEY='jabberwocky-phase5-posting';
      const PREVIOUS_KEY='jabberwocky-phase4-posting';
      const sites=Object.fromEntries(siteData.map((site)=>[site.id,site]));
      const select=document.getElementById('phase5-continent');
      const previous=document.getElementById('previous-team');
      const needed=document.getElementById('assignment-needed');
      const message=document.getElementById('save-message');
      const show=(id,announce=false)=>{
        const site=sites[id];
        if(!site){previous.hidden=true;needed.hidden=false;message.textContent='';return;}
        localStorage.setItem(KEY,id);previous.hidden=false;needed.hidden=true;
        document.getElementById('briefing-continent').textContent=`${site.icon} ${site.name}`;
        document.getElementById('briefing-surface').textContent=site.previousTeamGeologicalBriefing.surfaceEnvironment;
        document.getElementById('briefing-structure').textContent=site.previousTeamGeologicalBriefing.structuralSiteNeed;
        document.getElementById('briefing-ground').textContent=site.previousTeamGeologicalBriefing.groundDisturbanceLimit;
        document.getElementById('briefing-question').textContent=site.previousTeamGeologicalBriefing.openGeologicalQuestion;
        const repeated=localStorage.getItem(PREVIOUS_KEY)===id;
        message.textContent=repeated?`⚠ ${site.name} matches the Phase 4 posting on this device. Use it only if your teacher intentionally reassigned it.`:(announce?`✓ ${site.name} saved for Phase 5 on this device.`:`Saved Phase 5 posting: ${site.name}`);
      };
      const saved=localStorage.getItem(KEY);if(saved&&sites[saved]){select.value=saved;show(saved,false);}select.addEventListener('change',()=>show(select.value,true));
    })();
  </script>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
:global(body){background:#08100d}.phase5-shell{max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 1rem 5rem;color:#eef3f0}.phase5-shell :global(.breadcrumbs){color:#94a19b}.phase5-shell :global(.breadcrumbs a){color:#dce7e1}:global(body:has(#phase5-hub) .jcec-submission-dock),:global(body:has(#phase5-hub) .jcec-device-tools){display:none!important}.eyebrow{margin:0;color:#e4b46e;font:850 .74rem/1.2 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.11em}.phase5-hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 270px;gap:1.5rem;align-items:end;margin:1rem 0;padding:clamp(1.5rem,4vw,2.6rem);border:1px solid #506059;border-radius:24px;background:radial-gradient(circle at 84% 14%,rgba(225,175,99,.16),transparent 28%),linear-gradient(145deg,#101915,#1c2a24)}.phase5-hero h1{margin:.55rem 0 .35rem;color:#fff;font-size:clamp(3rem,8vw,5.6rem);line-height:.88;letter-spacing:-.055em}.phase5-hero h1 span{display:block;color:#e7b66d}.division{margin:.65rem 0 0;color:#f3d3a5;font-size:.75rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em}.lead{max-width:760px;margin:.9rem 0 0;color:#c3cec8;font-size:1.03rem;line-height:1.6}.phase5-hero aside{display:grid;gap:.18rem;padding:1rem;border:1px solid #58675f;border-radius:14px;background:#0d1612}.phase5-hero aside span{color:#e4b46e;font-size:.7rem;font-weight:900}.phase5-hero aside strong{color:#fff;font-size:1.15rem}.phase5-hero aside small{color:#99a69f}.big-question{margin:1rem 0;padding:1.2rem;border-left:4px solid #e4b46e;border-radius:0 14px 14px 0;background:#142019}.big-question span{color:#e4b46e;font-size:.7rem;font-weight:900}.big-question h2{margin:.35rem 0;color:#fff;font-size:clamp(1.3rem,3vw,1.9rem)}.big-question p{margin:.5rem 0 0;color:#9fada6}.posting-panel{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr .8fr;gap:1rem;margin:1.2rem 0;padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid #4a5a52;border-radius:17px;background:#111b17}.posting-panel h2{margin:.3rem 0;color:#fff}.posting-panel p{color:#a9b6b0}.assignment-control{display:grid;gap:.45rem;padding:1rem;border:1px solid #4d5d55;border-radius:12px;background:#0b1410}.assignment-control label{display:grid;gap:.15rem}.assignment-control strong{color:#fff}.assignment-control span{color:#919f98;font-size:.78rem}.assignment-control select{padding:.72rem;border:1px solid #63716a;border-radius:8px;background:#17221d;color:#fff}.assignment-control p{margin:0;color:#efc787;font-size:.76rem}.previous-team,.evidence-system,.how-it-works,.mission-list{margin:1.3rem 0;padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid #435149;border-radius:18px;background:#101915}.briefing-heading{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;align-items:end}.briefing-heading h2,.section-heading h2{margin:.28rem 0 .8rem;color:#fff}.briefing-heading>strong{padding:.4rem .6rem;border-radius:999px;background:#26372f}.briefing-intro{color:#9ba9a2}.briefing-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:.65rem}.briefing-grid article{padding:.9rem;border:1px solid #425149;border-radius:12px;background:#0a120f}.briefing-grid small{color:#e4b46e;font-size:.64rem;font-weight:900}.briefing-grid p{color:#c3cec8;font-size:.83rem;line-height:1.47}.continue-strip{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;align-items:center;margin-top:.8rem;padding:.8rem;border-radius:11px;background:#1a2922}.continue-strip div{display:grid;gap:.15rem}.continue-strip strong{color:#fff}.continue-strip span{color:#9aa8a1;font-size:.8rem}.continue-strip a,.mission-ready-link{padding:.7rem .85rem;border-radius:9px;background:#e4b46e;color:#2a1b08!important;text-decoration:none;font-size:.81rem;font-weight:900;white-space:nowrap}.quick-start{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;align-items:center;margin:1.2rem 0;padding:1rem;border:1px dashed #5b6962;border-radius:14px;background:#101915}.quick-start h2{margin:.2rem 0;color:#fff}.quick-start p{color:#99a69f}.quick-start>span{display:grid;place-items:center;width:55px;height:55px;border-radius:50%;background:#e4b46e;color:#281a08;font-size:1.35rem;font-weight:950}.evidence-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.7rem}.evidence-grid article{padding:1rem;border-radius:13px}.evidence-grid small{font-size:.64rem;font-weight:900}.evidence-grid h3{margin:.25rem 0;color:#fff}.evidence-grid p{margin:.35rem 0 0;line-height:1.5}.evidence-grid .earth{border:1px solid #527b91;background:#10222c}.evidence-grid .earth small{color:#8fd2f4}.evidence-grid .earth p{color:#b9d1dd}.evidence-grid .jabber{border:1px solid #81643a;background:#281f12}.evidence-grid .jabber small{color:#efc987}.evidence-grid .jabber p{color:#d9c8aa}.evidence-rule{display:grid;gap:.2rem;margin-top:.7rem;padding:.8rem;border-radius:10px;background:#1a2420}.evidence-rule strong{color:#d6edf1}.evidence-rule span{color:#e8d1a6}.evidence-rule b{margin-top:.25rem;color:#fff;font-size:.8rem}.work-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:.65rem}.work-grid article{display:flex;gap:.65rem;padding:.85rem;border:1px solid #414f48;border-radius:11px;background:#0b1310}.work-grid strong{color:#fff}.work-grid p{margin:.2rem 0 0;color:#96a39d;font-size:.78rem}.sequence-strip{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:.7rem 0 1rem;padding:.7rem;border-radius:10px;background:#0a120f}.sequence-strip span{padding:.35rem .5rem;border-radius:7px;color:#8d9993;font-size:.74rem;font-weight:900}.sequence-strip .current{background:#392b17;color:#ffd494}.sequence-strip b{color:#59655f}.mission-cards{display:grid;gap:.65rem}.mission-card{display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px 1fr auto;gap:.8rem;align-items:center;padding:.9rem;border:1px solid #3f4d46;border-radius:12px;background:#0b1310}.mission-card.current{border-color:#a77b3d;background:#1d1810}.mission-card.locked{opacity:.76}.mission-icon{font-size:1.5rem}.mission-topline{display:flex;gap:.5rem;align-items:center}.mission-topline span{color:#e4b46e;font-size:.62rem;font-weight:900}.mission-topline b{color:#89958f;font-size:.61rem}.mission-card h3{margin:.15rem 0;color:#fff}.mission-question{margin:.2rem 0;color:#c5d0ca;font-size:.85rem}.mission-summary{margin:.15rem 0 0;color:#89978f;font-size:.76rem}.mission-locked{color:#7e8a84;font-size:.76rem;font-weight:850}.phase4-link{display:grid;grid-template-columns:32px 1fr auto;gap:.7rem;align-items:center;margin-top:1.2rem;padding:.9rem;border:1px solid #3f4d46;border-radius:12px;background:#0c1411}.phase4-link>span{color:#e4b46e;font-size:1.25rem}.phase4-link strong{color:#fff}.phase4-link p{margin:.2rem 0 0;color:#8f9d95;font-size:.76rem}.phase4-link a{color:#efc887;font-size:.78rem;font-weight:850}
@media(max-width:850px){.phase5-hero,.posting-panel{grid-template-columns:1fr}.briefing-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.mission-card{grid-template-columns:48px 1fr}.mission-card>a,.mission-locked{grid-column:2}}
@media(max-width:620px){.briefing-grid,.work-grid,.evidence-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.continue-strip{display:grid}.continue-strip a{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;text-align:center}.mission-card{grid-template-columns:42px 1fr}.phase4-link{grid-template-columns:28px 1fr}.phase4-link a{grid-column:2}.sequence-strip{justify-content:flex-start}.posting-panel{padding:1rem}}
</style>
